\subsection*{Bifurcation Engine}

Given the FTL state $\mathbf{X}_{n}$, the bifurcation engine defines
\[
\mathcal{B} : \mathbf{X}_{n} \mapsto \{\mathbf{X}^{(k)}_{n+1}\}_{k=1}^{N},
\]
such that
\[
\mathbf{X}^{(k)}_{n+1} = \mathcal{F}_{k}(\mathbf{X}_{n}, \Delta t),
\]
with branch selection governed by a bifurcation condition
\[
\beta(\mathbf{X}_{n}) =
\begin{cases}
\text{single-branch}, & (G,\Sigma) \notin \mathcal{C}_{\text{crit}}, \\
\text{multi-branch}, & (G,\Sigma) \in \mathcal{C}_{\text{crit}}.
\end{cases}
\]
Each branch $k$ is associated with a distinct engine profile $\mathcal{F}_{k}$ (e.g. safe, extreme, exploratory),
and each resulting state $\mathbf{X}^{(k)}_{n+1}$ is recorded in the sovereign ledger as a separate FTL event.